# Golden files are generator OUTPUT, not source. Formatting them is
# wrong by definition: the test renders with JSON.stringify(x, null, 2)
# and compares byte-for-byte, and Prettier's printWidth:100 collapses
# short arrays onto one line — a shape JSON.stringify can never emit.
#
# So the pre-commit hook (lint-staged runs `prettier --write` over
# **/*.json) reformatted these under the commit that added them, and the
# suite went red the moment it landed. Regenerating would have been
# green until exactly the next commit.
#
# The whole directory, not the two files that happened to fail:
# golden.phenopacket.json and golden.fhir-r4.json pass today only
# because neither currently holds an array short enough to collapse.
#
# This file covers the hook and nothing else. Prettier 3 resolves the
# ignore file against its CWD and does not walk up to the repo root, so
# `npm run format` — CWD apps/api, both under npm workspaces and in CI's
# api job — never loaded this file and listed both golden.treat-nmd*.json.
# apps/api/.prettierignore is the counterpart that covers that invocation;
# the two lists have to stay in step, and apps/api/src/format-ignore.test.ts
# runs prettier from both directories to make sure they do.
apps/api/src/modules/patient-profile/export/__fixtures__/golden.*.json
